SM(574,{"n":"1 Thessalonians 2","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/1 Thessalonians 2.mp3","d":2406.4,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest, serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.92,"Okay, we'll go ahead and get started in St."],[25.04,"Paul's first Epistle to the Thessalonians, chapter 2, verse 1."],[31.84,"For you yourselves know, brethren, that our coming to you was not in vain."],[38.24,"But even after we had suffered before and were spitefully treated at Philippi, as you know, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God in much conflict."],[49.92,"For our exhortation did not come from error or uncleanness, nor was it in deceit."],[57.28,"So this, if nothing else, makes clear that St."],[59.84,"Paul is writing this not that long after he was there"],[63.3,"So this is another reason for believing this is fairly early in terms of uh Saint Paul's epistles."],[69.14,"We said last time how he was probably writing this from Corinth during the years that he spent in Corinth, writing back to uh Thessalonica."],[78.82,"And so he mentions here those events in Acts."],[81.78,"Remember, in Philippi he had been in had been thrown in prison, uh, and there was that earthquake in the middle of the night in the Philippian jailer."],[90.5,"That story, and so he mentions that, the way they were treated at Philippi, being thrown in prison and all that."],[96.34,"Then when they came to Thessalonica, there was the conflict in Thessalonica with the uh leaders of the synagogue there."],[104.18,"And so St"],[105.4,"Paul is uh referring back to that."],[108.77,"So he's saying, when we came to you, meaning when he came and preached the gospel there, and helped establish this Christian community, saying it's not in vain, even though, it was it was not the best of times."],[123.58,"It was more the worst of times."],[125.12,"There was a lot going on, but it was still not in vain."],[129.68,"Verse 3, 4, meaning because our exhortation did not come from error or uncleanness, nor was it in deceit."],[137.45,"So even though there were a lot of people trying to find fault with them, trying to persecute them, trying to drive them out of town, trying to discourage them from going and preaching the gospel, because their preaching wasn't coming from these other possible motives."],[156.07,"Error or uncleanness or deceit."],[158.77,"They weren't there for money, they weren't there for power, they weren't there for right for the wrong reasons."],[163.49,"If they had been there for those reasons, then when they had all that trouble, they would have gone home."],[171.03,"They would have said, forget this."],[173.59,"This isn't this the scam isn't working out how we planned."],[176.73,"And they would have given it up."],[178.17,"But that's not why they were there."],[179.69,"And so even though they faced that."],[182.1,"They continued and they pressed on because what they were doing was was more important than that."],[187.1,"And that shows the quality and the importance of the gospel that they preached there, that they were willing to go through all of that suffering and all of that difficulty to do it."],[200.34,"Verse 4 But as we have been approved by God to be entrusted with the gospel, even so we speak not as pleasing men, but God who tests our hearts."],[222.98,"So it's more that, God God gave them this task."],[227.53,"God is the one who assigned this to them."],[230.57,"And what he assigned to them was he gave them the gospel."],[233.37,"And trusted it to them and said, Go and go and preach it"],[240.43,"Right. So they've been given this charge by God Himself."],[244.09,"And so St."],[244.89,"Paul's saying, so we're not worried about what humans think of us."],[250.42,"We're not working for the people of Philippi."],[252.82,"We're not working for the members of the synagogue in Thessalonica."],[257.2,"That's not who we're working for, that's not who we're serving, that's not who we're trying to impress."],[261.62,"It's God Himself who gave us this task, gave us this charge, trusted us with this."],[266.58,"He's the one who we're concerned about."],[270.02,"He's the one who doesn't just look for results."],[275.24,"But as St."],[275.8,"Paul says, he tests our hearts."],[276.04,"s So he know why we're doing it and what our motives are and what we care about and what we love and what's important to us."],[289.02,"Verse 5: for neither at any time did we use flattering words, as you know, nor a cloak for covetousness."],[296.78,"God is witness."],[307.18,"And try and flatter people and try and do that."],[311.02,"They didn't, they didn't uh you know, a cloak for covetousness, meaning we weren't secretly out for money, and pretending, oh no, we're men of God, we're we're missionaries, when really what they wanted was cash."],[326.12,"They do either of those, and he said, God is our witness."],[329.37,"God knows. And you know."],[332.3,"So remember, in in the Torah in the Old Testament, you called two witnesses to prove something."],[339.2,"So he's saying, You know that we didn't do that, God knows we didn't do that."],[342.8,"That means it's true."],[344.17,"There's two witnesses."],[347.77,"For six, nor did we seek glory from men, either from you or from others, when we might have made demands as apostles of Christ."],[355.99,"So you say we didn't come to get to be famous, to be loved, to be propped up. as leaders, and have everybody say how great we were and how wise we were and all of this"],[368.87,"Right. And he says, not only not from the people of the city, but not even from you."],[375.37,"From the Christians, the Christians who are their disciples."],[378.73,"They're like, that's not what we're looking for from you either."],[381.78,"Because St. Paul wants them to be following Christ, not following St."],[384.98,"Paul. It's not about St."],[386.84,"Paul for Saint Paul."],[390.52,"Verse 7. But we were gentle among you, just as a nursing mother cherishes her own children."],[398.68,"So he compares the way he treated them and interacted with them in the Christian community as the way a mother nurses her baby, and holds and cares for her baby."],[411.72,"So this is more of the imagery that we've seen St."],[414.76,"Paul use in other epistles."],[416.3,"He talks about the um the new Christians."],[422.79,"Especially the ones who have come from paganism and just been baptized and just come into a whole new religious world, as being like infants in the faith."],[430.55,"They've been born again, so now they're babies."],[432.81,"And they need to grow."],[434.09,"And so appropriately then he treats them in this parental way."],[440.83,"This nurturing way, where he loves them and cares about them."],[445.04,"This is the antithesis of the other things he was. describing"],[449.49,"A nursing mother with a baby is not trying to get money out of the baby."],[453.78,"It's not trying to get complimented by the baby, it's not trying to get glory for the baby."],[458.58,"The baby can't give mom anything at that point."],[462.32,"Baby is dependent on mom for everything."],[465.12,"And the mom is just giving to the baby to provide the baby with what the baby needs out of love."],[470.9,"And so that's that's the imagery St."],[473.06,"Paul is using to give the opposite."],[475.08,"The exact opposite of why some people might come to you, and preach things, is why we came."],[484.22,"Verse 8, so affectionately longing for you, we were well pleased to impart to you not only the gospel of God, but also our own lives, because you had become dear to us."],[499.62,"So he says, We preach to you the gospel of God."],[503.15,"The victory of God in Christ."],[505.55,"We preach that to you, but we didn't just give you that, but he says we gave you our own lives."],[511.57,"Now that's not he gave them their life."],[513.73,"I mean, he's not dead."],[514.95,"So he's not saying he died for them."],[517.45,"And then he keeps saying we, because remember, this is coming from Saint Paul, St."],[523.93,"Sylvanus, and Saint Timothy."],[527.23,"There's two co-authors listed on this."],[529.07,"But St. Paul and his companions."],[531.0,"He's saying they gave their lives to them."],[532.2,"As opposed to for them"],[535.98,"Well, what does that mean?"],[536.86,"That means he invested some of his life in them."],[539.98,"How long was he there?"],[541.9,"He was there for some months."],[543.9,"Um, but that's a piece of his life."],[549.36,"That that he that he gave to them."],[551.36,"And Saint Paul has talked this way before that we've seen."],[554.1,"When he referred to one of his churches as sort of his letters of recommendation, like that, they're his C V."],[561.16,"They're what he has to show for his work at the end of the day."],[565.65,"When when it's St."],[567.41,"Paul gets to the end of his life, when he's executed in Rome, what he has to point to in terms of his life's work are those churches, those different cities, and those people in those communities who he gave his life to and spent his time with, teaching and instructing and loving them and sharing his life with them and their lives with him."],[589.93,"We talked about how he's in Corinth for years while he's writing this."],[593.37,"He's at people's weddings, he's baptizing people's babies, he's right, he's doing all of these things."],[599.21,"He's doing funerals."],[600.67,"Effectively. He's there at their funerals."],[602.83,"He's part of their lives and he's giving part of his life to them every time he does that."],[610.72,"And um this is this is something we don't think about as much, I think, in the modern world because uh we spend so much time wasting our time that we don't see it as valuable anymore right we're perfectly happy to like sit and veg on a couch and you know watch Netflix or flip through channels and watch nothing in particular you know and and just sort of let hours go by of our lives and fritter them away on nothing you know um and all retirement and and since we do that, since we've gotten so used to doing I mean from the time we're kids."],[658.7,"Now our kids are all entertained, you know, 24-7."],[662.46,"And so you grow up that way and you just keep enter trying to entertain yourself all the time."],[667.36,"So that you can't now we're at the point where um since I went back to having a flip phone, uh, I am now a serious conversational terrorist."],[677.6,"Because I'll like sit down to eat and just like stare at a person and expect them to talk to me."],[683.44,"Which people aren't used to anymore."],[685.36,"Like they'll want to get on their phone, but then like I don't have a phone to get on, so then they feel awkward, so they have to put the phone down and they don't know what to do anymore."],[695.36,"So like we've we've sort of lost that."],[698.16,"We're so used to just constantly being entertained by something, you know, or having a TV on, or having a radio on, and having noise and having five things going on."],[707.76,"St Paul obviously is before most of that, but he also has a different sense in terms of his life."],[720.25,"And that just as Christ entrusted him with the gospel, Christ also entrusted him with a certain number of years on this earth that are made up of a certain number of days and a certain number of hours and a certain number of minutes."],[737.05,"And that he's a steward of that."],[741.05,"And that not only does he not want to waste that, but he wants to invest it."],[746.33,"it. Um, we probably all know somebody, if we don't want to admit's us, who wastes money"],[754.99,"That's uh you don't know anybody."],[760.67,"Okay, okay. But I am."],[763.95,"So uh we probably who just goes and every penny they get they go and spend on something, usually something dumb."],[771.73,"Or something inconsequential, or just entertainment."],[775.15,"And they just fritter it away and fritter it away and f and fritter it away."],[778.99,"And none of us look at that person and say, Well, that person is really wise."],[782.67,"Like that person is really good with money."],[785.2,"The person who we think is good with money is the person who we see who takes money and invests it, invests it."],[791.38,"And uses it wisely."],[793.82,"But the same is true with time."],[796.94,"And we tend to look at time the exact opposite way."],[799.82,"We think the person who's going out and having fun all the time is making wise use of time."],[806.54,"And that's the opposite."],[809.0,"The person who's wise with time is the person who invests it."],[812.84,"And the most wise thing you can invest your time in, your time on this earth in, is other people."],[821.45,"Because all the other stuff you can invest your time in is going to cease to exist."],[830.01,"You can spend your whole life building a magnificent building, and hundreds of years from now, it'll be a pile of dust."],[837.21,"They're all gonna die"],[837.86,"That's you can invest your time, all kinds of things in this world."],[843.14,"The only thing in this world that's going to go on into eternity is other people."],[849.62,"And so St."],[850.34,"Paul understands this."],[852.26,"And that's why he's willing and able to go to Thessalonica and invest his time and himself and his life in the people there."],[864.02,"And then go to Corinth and invest himself in the people there."],[869.31,"And show them how to do that with each other."],[872.81,"And with the other people in their community."],[875.81,"Um so we can't rotate the clock back."],[881.09,"We might think it would be nice."],[883.11,"Like to just all throw away our cell phones and smash all our TVs and get rid of our computers and the internet and all that stuff, and then we wouldn't be tempted to waste time, and then we'd have to do you know better things with our time."],[895.35,"Try and force ourselves, but uh we can't do that."],[898.63,"It's not gonna work."],[900.55,"There's too many ways to waste time if we want to, but we can try to get back to looking at our time and looking at our lives at least more like St."],[909.89,"Paul did and and is encouraging us to."],[914.13,"Verse 9, for you remember, brethren, our labor and toil, for laboring night and day that we might not be a burden to any of you."],[922.37,"We preached you to you the gospel of God."],[924.77,"So this is St"],[927.61,"Paul talking about how not only was he working with them and preaching to them and part of their worship and prayer together and all of this, but they were also working working."],[940.09,"They were also paying their own way so that they didn't have to ask the people of Thessalonica for money."],[949.13,"Why is St."],[949.85,"Paul doing that?"],[950.57,"Because we've seen St."],[951.37,"Paul say other places that they need to be supporting the leadership of the churches."],[957.59,"Financially. He's told the people they should be."],[960.23,"So why didn't Paul tell them that about himself?"],[962.63,"Well, because he wanted it to be clear what he was saying before."],[966.19,"That he wasn't there for the money."],[969.52,"And if he came in there telling them, oh, by the way, I need you to support me while I preach this to you and teach you about this."],[979.01,"Then they would have all said, Oh, well, we know what this is."],[983.11,"This is the self-help seminar that costs, you know, $800 and this guy goes town from town."],[988.15,"This is his grift."],[989.53,"Um, and so St."],[991.37,"Paul went extra, to make sure that they would never think that."],[997.84,"They would never think that."],[1001.28,"Verse 10, you are witnesses and God also, see, two witnesses again."],[1006.28,"How devoutly and justly and blamelessly we behaved ourselves among you who believe."],[1012.52,"As you know how we exhorted and comforted and charged every one of you as a father does his own children, that you would walk worthy of God who calls you into his own kingdom and glory."],[1025.56,"So he says, You saw how we lived our lives."],[1028.44,"You know how we encouraged you to live your lives."],[1032.46,"And that's this image now of a father in children."],[1035.6,"This is yet another place where Saint Paul refers to himself as the father of one of his churches."],[1043.88,"Just for when one of our friends asks us, well, doesn't the Bible say you're not supposed to call yourself father if you're a leader in the church?"],[1052.12,"And you say, Well, St."],[1053.16,"Paul did all the time."],[1055.72,"I don't think he was sinning when he did that in the Bible."],[1058.76,"So, but um, but what is a what does a father try to do with his kids when he's raising his kids?"],[1066.6,"He tries to teach them how to live their lives."],[1069.45,"Here's how you grow up, here's how you be a man or a woman."],[1072.51,"Here's how you conduct yourself, here's what you do."],[1075.0,"And Saint Paul's saying, we did that both ways by doing it ourselves when we live there, and by encouraging you and comforting you and exhorting you and and to to live that way yourselves."],[1088.04,"And um, that's that walk."],[1092.3,"We've seen St."],[1093.02,"Paul use that imagery before."],[1095.84,"If you're on this journey, you're walking."],[1098.8,"To come to the kingdom of God and glory and his glory."],[1105.37,"That's what's at the end of the road."],[1107.83,"And so that's the trip you're taking."],[1110.63,"And we're telling you how to how to do that and showing you how to do that by our example."],[1117.03,"Um, this is one of the rare places."],[1121.27,"I've commented before I know that there are certain folks who want to separate Saint Paul from Christ."],[1130.71,"They want to say, oh, well, when you look at the Gospels and you see how Christ speaks in the Gospels, and then you look at St."],[1135.83,"Paul and how St."],[1136.47,"Paul died, it's totally different."],[1139.21,"Jesus is saying these nice things and parables and encouraging everything."],[1143.41,"Then St. Paul comes with all his theology and doctrine and blah blah blah."],[1147.3,"Um we've seen a bunch of times how that's not true."],[1150.18,"But one of the big things that they always throw in there."],[1153.8,"Their exhibit A is they'll say that, well, Christ came and talked about the kingdom of God all the time."],[1160.04,"Or the kingdom of heaven."],[1161.8,"St. Paul doesn't talk about that, except here."],[1165.4,"But at a couple other places."],[1168.12,"But so I wanted to point that out just because this is yet another place where no, they're really saying the same thing."],[1175.81,"And here they're even using the same words."],[1178.13,"It's not just me saying, well, what St."],[1180.13,"Paul means by this is really the same kind of idea as kingdom."],[1183.65,"No, this is he's using the word."],[1192.06,"Verse 13. For this reason we also thank God without ceasing, because when you receive the word of God which you heard from us, you welcomed it not as the word of men, but as it is in truth the word of God, which also effectively works in you who believe."],[1214.42,"says, here's another, He he's been giving this list of all the things he's happy about."],[1218.54,"This is sort of like Philippians, in that St."],[1221.1,"Paul is this is a pretty positive, report to the Thessalonians."],[1226.96,"Because he's heard these reports about since he's left, he's heard these things about how things are going, and he's hearing good things."],[1232.58,"So now here's another thing he's rejoicing in that they didn't just hear what St."],[1238.02,"Paul had to say as well."],[1240.58,"That Paul guy has some good ideas."],[1242.98,"You know, I'll take that under consideration."],[1245.38,"You know, here's some wise sayings."],[1247.94,"I'll I'll uh you know throw that in the repertoire."],[1250.34,"But they received it as what he's preaching is coming to us from God."],[1255.8,"This is the account of God's victory, and this isn't his philosophy or self-help program or cult that he's starting, or right, whatever."],[1264.36,"This isn't coming from St."],[1266.2,"Paul or any or his companions or any other men."],[1269.48,"There's not a bunch of guys back in Jerusalem who sent these guys out to sell Amway."],[1274.41,"This is this is coming to them directly from God, and that's how they received it."],[1280.73,"Question. Yes, sir."],[1282.49,"Um uses this phrase, in you who believe, this sounds like he's making belief."],[1292.97,"We've talked about this lots of times."],[1294.65,"It sounds like he's making belief in certain propositions, the price of admission."],[1302.54,"And so can you explain?"],[1305.18,"I know that he isn't."],[1307.32,"So the better translation of that would be uh, because it's a verb, would be in you who are faithful."],[1314.76,"Okay, so it's a translation?"],[1315.48,"s So the word that get translated, believe, faith, faithful, and faithfulness in the New Testament are all the same word in Greek."],[1316.88,"Yes. Yes. And so it gets translated different ways, usually to try to bring out the theological perspective of the translators."],[1341.5,"And since we're working with the New King James, you can guess as to what that might be."],[1347.66,"But yes, so this would be right."],[1351.98,"The faithful. And this is what we use, like you'll hear this in the liturgy."],[1356.14,"When we refer to the people, we don't say believers."],[1360.06,"We say the faithful"],[1362.18,"Let us the faithful pray for the catechumens."],[1366.84,"So the when I was a Protestant, it was the believers a lot of it."],[1371.08,"Yeah. Yeah. So."],[1377.0,"Yeah. And so, I mean, the word belief used to have more to it than true false test."],[1384.49,"Just I accept the truth of that statement is sort of what believe means now."],[1391.11,"Whereas um. And that version of belief doesn't work with, for example, the man who tells Christ, I believe, Lord, help my unbelief."],[1402.37,"That makes no sense if it's just I accept that that is true"],[1403.37,"Yeah. Help me accept that that is true because I also don't."],[1414.99,"Like that makes literally no sense."],[1418.72,"But if he's what he's saying is, I want to be faithful, help my unfaithfulness."],[1424.62,"I want to trust, help my lack of trust."],[1428.06,"That makes a lot of sense."],[1429.76,"I trust you, help my lack of trust."],[1432.08,"That makes perfect sense."],[1436.73,"Um, because there's a lot more to faithfulness or trust or loyalty than just mi uh making a flip in your brain."],[1449.46,"The only survival, I guess, of that in our use of belief now, is if I say, Well, I believe in you."],[1455.62,"Yes. I'm not saying I think you're really true."],[1460.34,"I acknowledge that you exist."],[1463.22,"You're saying trust."],[1466.4,"And and and it was that way for a long way in English."],[1468.56,"When someone said, I believe in Jesus, they didn't mean mean I believe that Jesus of Nazareth historically existed."],[1477.34,"That's not what they meant."],[1478.94,"They meant more than that."],[1481.08,"They meant more than that."],[1482.97,"The same thing with faith, really right faith now is just sort of accepting the truth of something but again I have faith in you right is that older meaning right I have faith in you doesn't just mean I accept that you are here right um yeah so it's more of that kind of right that there's there's this active sense right and so because they are faithful right St."],[1514.45,"Paul is saying because you're faithful, because you've received the gospel in this way, Christ is working in you."],[1523.45,"Verse 14. For you, brethren became imitators of the churches of God which are in Judea in Christ Jesus."],[1530.81,"For you also suffered the same things from your own countrymen, just as they did from the Judeans, who killed both the Lord Jesus and their own prophets, and have persecuted us, and they did not please God and are contrary to all men."],[1549.13,"Before we say St."],[1550.01,"Paul is anti-Semitic, let's remember."],[1552.17,"He's a Judean too."],[1553.93,"So um. So um it's interesting, you know, almost every other place in the New King James Version, I have to comment."],[1564.73,"Almost every other place in the New King James Version, they translate the word Judean as Jew."],[1569.53,"You notice here they left it Judean."],[1573.13,"Because if they translated it Jew, it would have sounded really horrible."],[1577.89,"And the reason it would have sounded really horrible is that if they'd translated it as Jew instead of Judean, we would have read all of our modern ethnic concepts and racial concepts back into it."],[1592.46,"Which are concepts that did not exist."],[1597.0,"We cannot forget it."],[1598.6,"Yeah, but these concepts did not exist in St."],[1602.2,"Paul's time. So St."],[1605.94,"Paul is talking about, he said, You became, he says, the way I know this, the way I know that Christ is working in you, and that way I know that you have received the gospel, not as right."],[1617.94,"as. He already said he didn't preach the gospel if it was a human message"],[1622.3,"He's saying the way I know you received it as coming from God is that you became like the churches in Judea."],[1629.1,"How? Well, not, oh well, you believe the same doctrines."],[1632.64,"You gave the same answers on the truefalse test."],[1636.0,"Um, not any of that kind of stuff."],[1639.04,"It's because you suffered persecution the way they they did."],[1643.84,"The way that they suffered persecution from their own countrymen."],[1646.8,"So the other Judeans who didn't accept Jesus as the Messiah, persecuted those who did."],[1654.06,"On the the um the same way these pagans now who have come into the uh come into the Christian community, the church in Thessalonica, have been persecuted by the former pagans."],[1671.72,"And so St."],[1672.68,"Paul talks about how, because this happened in Thessalonica, how they've also been, his own people have been persecuting him."],[1680.12,"And um think about how they do not please God and are contrary to all men."],[1688.52,"So what does it mean that they don't please God?"],[1690.44,"Well, remember what Christ said to his disciples in St."],[1693.88,"John's Gospel before he was crucified."],[1696.2,"He said, The time will come when people will think they're doing service to God by killing you."],[1702.25,"They'll think they're pleasing God by coming and hunting you.ing you down and kill"],[1706.29,"And who was one of the people who was doing that?"],[1710.61,"Saul of Tarsus."],[1713.15,"So St. Paul knows this firsthand."],[1716.77,"So when he says they don't please God, this is what he's talking about."],[1720.77,"He knows it firsthand."],[1722.13,"He knows he was not pleased."],[1723.49,"He thought he was."],[1725.66,"He thought he was being really pious and zealous for God when he was out there persecuting Christians and killing them and rounding them up."],[1733.92,"But he he wasn't."],[1735.04,"And so he's saying, and they're not."],[1737.08,"Even though they think they are."],[1740.18,"And the contrary to all men is what they're doing, is actually putting them at enmity, not just with God, but with their fellow man."],[1750.04,"Because what does their fellow man need to hear the gospel?"],[1753.08,"And they're trying to stop it."],[1755.88,"Because they've rejected it."],[1759.29,"Um. So that's what that's what uh St."],[1763.69,"Paul is aiming at."],[1765.05,"And this was not something."],[1767.58,"Again, we want to read this ethnic and racial stuff back into it."],[1773.34,"This is not Saint Paul, like attacking and criticizing even his own group."],[1780.88,"And trying to put himself as superior to them, or someone the Christians as superior to them."],[1787.66,"This is a this was a top.ic, as we saw in Romans, of great pain to Saint Paul"],[1794.74,"The fact that this was true."],[1806.18,"Meaning he said he would go to hell himself if it would mean saving his fellow Jews coming to Christ."],[1814.34,"That's how much he loved them."],[1816.42,"That's how much it pained him that they hadn't accepted the Messiah when he came."],[1820.74,"So St. Paul's not like delighting in this."],[1824.76,"In saying this."],[1825.9,"This is the sad truth from St."],[1827.58,"Paul's perspective. And he's hopeful that it will change."],[1831.95,"But until then, just like he did before the road to Damascus, they've made themselves an obstacle to the grace of God and to the gospel going out."],[1842.63,"These Judeans who haven't accepted Jesus as the Messiah."],[1851.51,"Verse 16, forbidding us to speak to the Gentiles that they may be saved."],[1856.23,"So as always to fill up the measure of their sins, but wrath has come upon them to the uttermost."],[1864.15,"So again, this is why."],[1869.35,"This is the core of the problem."],[1871.03,"This is why they're contrary to all men."],[1873.51,"Because they're trying to stop Saint Paul from preaching the gospel to the nations."],[1877.67,"They're trying to stop people from hearing about Christ"],[1882.83,"And when you do that, we've talked before about how God's wrath is what happens when you're on the wrong side of him."],[1894.51,"It's not St."],[1895.23,"Paul saying God's really angry at them."],[1898.51,"God's gonna smash them."],[1902.03,"That's not what God's wrath is."],[1905.13,"God is doing something in the world."],[1907.77,"We've talked about this."],[1908.65,"This is what the fathers talk about with the divine energies."],[1910.97,"God is at work in the world."],[1912.57,"He's transforming the world, he's bringing the world to salvation, he's transfiguring it."],[1917.35,"That includes people."],[1919.61,"And so you can imagine that as like this rushing river."],[1923.01,"What's going to happen if you try to fight against the current of a rushing river?"],[1929.09,"It's going to tear you apart."],[1932.15,"Whereas if you go with the current, it will carry you along."],[1936.36,"So that's the idea that's in, as we've seen before, you know, going back to Romans where it talked about God's wrath."],[1943.16,"That's what St."],[1943.8,"Paul has in his mind in terms of God's wrath."],[1945.66,"So again, he's not gloating."],[1946.86,"He's not, oh, God's gonna get you."],[1949.5,"You know good, mimic"],[1952.24,"That's not what St."],[1953.12,"Paul's aiming at."],[1954.0,"But he's saying they're now suffering, because he says they're already suffering it."],[1960.72,"They're already suffering it."],[1962.98,"This has consequences in your life when you're trying to fight against God."],[1967.14,"And you're trying to fight against what God is doing in the world, and you're trying to fight against what God wants to do in you."],[1972.34,"And again, St."],[1973.14,"Paul knows that because he was there."],[1977.23,"Not that many years before that."],[1979.63,"Before this. If this is written 5051, then like 15 years before this, he was out doing that."],[1989.11,"So that's that's what he's talking about."],[1992.17,"He doesn't think that's the end of their story."],[1995.21,"He doesn't say this is the way it's gonna be for all of their descendants until the end of time."],[2001.15,"He's not telling the Thessalonians that they need to go out and do something to them."],[2007.27,"He's saying these, and why is he talking about them?"],[2011.35,"Remember, this whole thing is part of an analogy."],[2015.43,"The Thessalonians are like the people who aren't doing that."],[2018.61,"The Thessalonians are like the Christians in Judea who are being persecuted by the Judeans, meaning the Thessalonians are being treated the same way by the pagans, and that means the pagans are in this same boat."],[2031.09,"Those pagans in Thessalonica who have it didn't accept St."],[2035.01,"Paul's preaching are in the same boat."],[2037.17,"So how does St."],[2038.13,"Paul want them to look at their fellow pagans who haven't heard the gospel yet?"],[2043.65,"The way he looks at his fellow Judeans."],[2046.21,"Which isn't as the enemy"],[2052.39,"Verse 17. But we, brethren, having been taken away from you for a short time in presence, not in heart, endeavored more eagerly to see your face with great desire."],[2066.63,"So he says, We've been away for a little while in terms of our face."],[2071.81,"We haven't seen each other face to face."],[2074.23,"He says, But my heart is still there."],[2076.63,"St. Paul left his heart in Thessalonica."],[2080.63,"But he says, My heart is still with you, and so he's saying, I I want to come back and visit you again."],[2089.99,"Verse 18, therefore we wanted to come to you, even I, Paul, time and again."],[2092.23,"even Why does he have to say I, Paul?"],[2092.47,"Look, Chris, remember there's three co-writers on this"],[2101.71,"Even I, Paul, time and again, but Satan hindered us."],[2107.47,"So he's saying, we've been wanting to come back and see you again, but things keep happening."],[2115.0,"Things keep going wrong."],[2116.44,"And so we haven't been able to."],[2121.32,"And so St."],[2122.04,"Paul is ascribing that to uh to Satan, making sure that things foul up and it and it doesn't quite happen."],[2130.68,"Notice that that uh what that perspective on Satan is."],[2137.58,"He doesn't talk about Satan like Satan's very scary."],[2141.1,"He talks about St."],[2142.38,"Paul here is talking about Satan like he's kind of a nuisance."],[2145.99,"Like, you know, like this is Satan in the sense of like, oh man, I lost my pen again."],[2155.12,"Oh man, I went to lit light the charcoal before Vespers and uh the altar servers used up the last of the matches and didn't tell me, so I had to go try and find a lighter."],[2163.78,"This is this is that kind of Satan."],[2166.27,"Just the annoying, irritating imp."],[2169.59,"right Right? Is how St."],[2170.75,"Paul's talking about him here."],[2172.27,"We keep having to change our travel plans because, you know, stuff goes wr.ong"],[2176.67,"Why would St"],[2179.59,"Paul be able to talk about Satan that way?"],[2183.75,"Christ already defeated him."],[2186.6,"He's got the big L."],[2188.28,"So he's the loser."],[2191.56,"So St. Paul could talk about that way because he was just talking about proclaiming the gospel, the victory of Christ, over Satan."],[2198.3,"So Satan's washed up."],[2200.78,"Well, would a Jew down to the nuisance level."],[2212.22,"Yeah, when you read in Second Temple literature, there's all these very, very scary devil faces, Azazel, uh Mastema."],[2220.0,"There's a whole bunch of them."],[2221.2,"The devil. The Satan, uh Satana L."],[2225.7,"There's a whole bunch of names for it, Belial."],[2227.94,"And yeah, they're always like the scary guy, the guy who's gonna have the big final showdown, you know, the big battle with the the forces of God at some point in the future, and sort of all this scary stuff, and uh yeah, that's not how St."],[2248.34,"Paul's looking at it."],[2249.14,"And even even when you get to the book of Revelation, like what is the dragon actually do?"],[2255.22,"What does he actually pull off and succeed at in the book of Revelation?"],[2260.9,"I don't know."],[2262.5,"He kind of gets I mean, he goes around trying to like trick and deceive people."],[2266.83,"And then he gets whooped on and tied up and thrown in a pit for a thousand years."],[2272.67,"You know, and then he gets let out for a little while and goes around trying to deceive people again, and then he gets grabbed and thrown into the lake of fire again."],[2281.09,"Like he's he's not super effective."],[2283.59,"Like if if you were making a superhero movie, this would not be a good villain."],[2287.61,"Everybody would criticize it."],[2289.67,"They'd be like, you need a villain that's a bigger challenge for your hero."],[2293.48,"If you're gonna write it, because there's there's no drama."],[2296.65,"But that's sort of the point."],[2298.09,"There is no drama."],[2299.83,"Like, it's over, it wasn't close."],[2303.05,"Like, um, that's it."],[2311.31,"Verse 19, for what is our hope or joy or crown of rejoicing?"],[2316.35,"Is it not even you in the presence of our Lord Jesus Christ at his coming?"],[2320.67,"For you are our glory and joy."],[2323.07,"This is getting back to that CV idea again."],[2325.96,"He says, So, what am I, St."],[2327.8,"Paul, gonna have to brag about in the end?"],[2331.02,"At the end of my life, what am I gonna have that I can brag about?"],[2333.58,"What am I gonna have that I can show off for what I did with my life?"],[2337.1,"And he said, It's gonna be you when you stand before Christ at his second coming."],[2342.96,"As being among the righteous."],[2344.48,"That's what I'm gonna have to show."],[2346.24,"That's gonna be the return on my investment of my time and my love and my care for you, is when that happens."],[2350.96,"Paul's working for"],[2353.42,"That's what St."],[2356.56,"And we've seen that St."],[2357.68,"Paul's attitude isn't is that, yes, he does try to work out work out his own salvation, but St."],[2365.52,"Paul in particular seems to be a lot more focused on other people's than his own."],[2369.77,"And when he does talk about his own, it's usually like, well, yeah, I continue to work too, because I don't want to help other people find salvation and not find it myself."],[2379.55,"But you notice which comes first in that example."],[2384.0,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2391.36,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancient faith.com."],[2392.8,"That's wholecouncil at ancient faithcom."]],"o":[{"t":21.92,"lv":2,"h":"1 Thessalonians 2:1-3 - Our coming was not in vain","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Starting <b>1 Thess 2:1</b>: \"our coming to you was <b>not in vain</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Mentions being <b>\"spitefully treated at Philippi\"</b> - Acts: <b>prison, earthquake, jailer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">shows Paul writing <b>not long after</b> he was there → another reason for <b>early date</b></li><li class=\"d1\">probably written from <b>Corinth</b>, back to Thessalonica</li><li class=\"d0\">Then <b>conflict in Thessalonica</b> with synagogue leaders</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not in vain\" even though it was \"<b>the worst of times</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v3</b>: exhortation not from <b>error, uncleanness, deceit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not there for <b>money, power</b>, wrong reasons</li><li class=\"d1\">if they were: when trouble came they'd have <b>gone home</b> - \"the scam isn't working\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they pressed on → shows <b>quality and importance of the gospel</b></li></ul>"},{"t":200.34,"lv":3,"h":"2:4-6 - Approved by God, not pleasing men","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v4</b>: \"approved by God to be <b>entrusted with the gospel</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God assigned</b> the task, handed them the gospel: \"go preach it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So not worried what humans think</li><li class=\"d1\">not working for <b>people of Philippi</b>, nor <b>synagogue members</b> in Thessalonica</li><li class=\"d1\">not trying to impress anyone</li><li class=\"d0\">God \"doesn't just look for <b>results</b>\" - he <b>tests our hearts</b>: knows motives, loves, what matters</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v5</b>: no <b>flattering words</b>, no <b>cloak for covetousness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not secretly out for <b>cash</b> while posing as \"men of God, missionaries\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>God is witness</b>\" - plus you know</li><li class=\"d1\">Torah: <b>two witnesses</b> prove a thing → so it's true</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v6</b>: not seeking <b>glory from men</b> - fame, being propped up as wise leaders</li><li class=\"d1\">not even from <b>you</b> (the disciples) - wants them following <b>Christ, not Paul</b></li></ul>"},{"t":390.52,"lv":2,"h":"2:7-8 - Gentle as a nursing mother","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v7</b>: \"gentle among you, as a <b>nursing mother</b> cherishes her own children\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Imagery Paul uses elsewhere: new Christians, esp. from <b>paganism</b>, = <b>infants in the faith</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"born again, so now they're babies\" - need to <b>grow</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so he treats them <b>parentally</b>, nurturing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Antithesis</b> of money / flattery / glory</li><li class=\"d1\">nursing mother not after <b>money</b>, <b>compliments</b>, <b>glory</b> from baby</li><li class=\"d1\">baby <b>dependent for everything</b>; mom gives out of <b>love</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Exact opposite of why some people might come and preach\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v8</b>: imparted not only <b>gospel of God</b> but \"<b>our own lives</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">gospel = <b>victory of God in Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"we\" = Paul, <b>Sylvanus</b>, <b>Timothy</b> (two co-authors)</li></ul>"},{"t":531.0,"lv":3,"h":"Giving your life to them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Gave lives <b>to them</b>, not <b>for them</b> - not dying for them</li><li class=\"d0\">Meant <b>investing part of his life</b> - there <b>some months</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Churches = his <b>letters of recommendation</b>, his <b>CV</b></li><li class=\"d1\">at end of life, executed in <b>Rome</b>, what he points to = <b>churches, communities, people</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Years in <b>Corinth</b>: at <b>weddings</b>, baptizing <b>babies</b>, <b>funerals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gives part of his life <b>every time</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Modern world doesn't think this way - we <b>waste time</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Netflix</b>, flipping channels, \"fritter them away on nothing\"</li><li class=\"d1\">kids entertained <b>24-7</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Aside: went back to a <b>flip phone</b> - now \"<b>conversational terrorist</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sit down to eat and <b>stare at a person</b> expecting them to talk</li><li class=\"d1\">people feel awkward - used to <b>constant entertainment, noise</b></li></ul>"},{"t":707.76,"lv":3,"h":"Time as stewardship - invest in people","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul sees his years as <b>entrusted by Christ</b> like the gospel</li><li class=\"d1\">certain number of <b>days, hours, minutes</b> - he's a <b>steward</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Doesn't want to <b>waste</b> it, wants to <b>invest</b> it</li><li class=\"d0\">Analogy: person who <b>wastes money</b> on dumb things - nobody calls them wise</li><li class=\"d1\">wise with money = one who <b>invests</b> it</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>same with time</b> - we look at it the opposite way</li><li class=\"d1\">\"person going out having fun all the time\" thought wise = <b>opposite</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Most wise investment = other people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">build a magnificent building → <b>pile of dust</b> in hundreds of years</li><li class=\"d1\">\"only thing that's going on into <b>eternity</b> is <b>other people</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So Paul invests in <b>Thessalonica</b>, then <b>Corinth</b>, teaches them to do it with each other</li><li class=\"d0\">Can't <b>rotate the clock back</b> - smash TVs, phones, internet: \"not gonna work\"</li><li class=\"d1\">try to look at our time <b>more like St. Paul</b></li></ul>"},{"t":914.13,"lv":2,"h":"2:9 - Working night and day","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v9</b>: \"laboring <b>night and day</b> that we might <b>not be a burden</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just teaching, worship, prayer - also <b>paying their own way</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Puzzle: Paul says elsewhere to <b>support church leadership financially</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so why not for himself?</li><li class=\"d1\">wanted it <b>clear he wasn't there for money</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if he'd said \"support me while I preach\" → \"<b>the $800 self-help seminar</b>, this is his <b>grift</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So went <b>extra</b> to be sure they'd never think that</li></ul>"},{"t":1001.28,"lv":2,"h":"2:10-12 - As a father with children","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v10</b>: \"you are <b>witnesses</b> and God also\" - <b>two witnesses</b> again</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>devoutly, justly, blamelessly</b> behaved</li><li class=\"d0\">You saw how we lived, how we encouraged you to live</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v11-12</b>: <b>exhorted, comforted, charged</b> as a <b>father</b> his children</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul calls himself <b>father</b> of his churches</li><li class=\"d1\">friend asks \"doesn't Bible say don't call leaders father?\" → \"<b>St. Paul did all the time</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">What does a father do? Teaches them <b>how to live</b>, be a man or woman</li><li class=\"d1\">did both: by <b>example</b> living there + by <b>exhorting</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>walk worthy of God</b>\" - journey imagery used before</li><li class=\"d1\">end of the road = <b>kingdom and glory</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1117.03,"lv":3,"h":"Paul and the kingdom of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Rare place: <b>Paul uses \"kingdom\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Folks who <b>separate Paul from Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Gospels: Jesus nice, <b>parables</b>; then Paul with \"theology and doctrine, blah blah\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"exhibit A\": <b>Christ talked kingdom of God</b> all the time, Paul <b>doesn't</b> (except here, a couple other places)</li><li class=\"d0\">Point: they say the <b>same thing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just \"same idea as kingdom\" - he uses <b>the word</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1192.06,"lv":2,"h":"2:13 - Received as the word of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v13</b>: thank God <b>without ceasing</b> - you welcomed it \"not as <b>word of men</b>\" but as <b>word of God</b>, which <b>works in you who believe</b></li><li class=\"d0\">List of things he's happy about - positive report like <b>Philippians</b></li><li class=\"d1\">heard good reports since leaving</li><li class=\"d0\">They didn't treat it as \"that Paul guy has some <b>good ideas</b>, wise sayings for the repertoire\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Received it as <b>God's victory account</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a <b>philosophy, self-help program, cult</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not from Paul or <b>guys back in Jerusalem</b> \"who sent these guys out to <b>sell Amway</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">coming <b>directly from God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1280.73,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: \"you who believe\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: phrase \"in you who believe\" - sounds like <b>belief in propositions</b> is price of admission?</li><li class=\"d0\">Better translation: \"you who are <b>faithful</b>\" - verb</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>believe, faith, faithful, faithfulness</b> = <b>same Greek word</b></li><li class=\"d1\">translators bring out <b>theological perspective</b> - \"New King James, guess what that might be\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Liturgy: \"<b>the faithful</b>\", not \"believers\" - \"Let us the faithful pray for the <b>catechumens</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Belief</b> used to be more than <b>true/false test</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>I believe, Lord, help my unbelief</b>\" makes no sense as \"accept as true\"</li><li class=\"d1\">as \"<b>I trust you, help my lack of trust</b>\" → perfect sense</li><li class=\"d1\">more to faithfulness, trust, <b>loyalty</b> than \"flip in your brain\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Survival: \"<b>I believe in you</b>\" / \"I have <b>faith in you</b>\" = trust, not acknowledging you exist</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I believe in Jesus\" didn't mean <b>historically existed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Active sense → because <b>faithful</b>, <b>Christ is working in you</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1523.45,"lv":2,"h":"2:14-15 - Imitators of the churches in Judea","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v14</b>: you became <b>imitators of the churches in Judea</b> - suffered same from <b>own countrymen</b>, as they from the <b>Judeans</b>, who killed Lord Jesus and prophets</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Before we say Paul is <b>anti-Semitic</b>\" - he's a <b>Judean too</b></li><li class=\"d0\">NKJV usually translates Judean as <b>\"Jew\"</b> - here left <b>Judean</b></li><li class=\"d1\">would sound horrible: we'd read <b>modern ethnic and racial concepts</b> back in - didn't exist in Paul's time</li><li class=\"d0\">How he knows Christ is working in them - <b>not</b> same doctrines, \"<b>true/false test</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but <b>same persecution</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Judeans who rejected Messiah persecuted believers ↔ <b>former pagans</b> persecute Thessalonian church</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul himself persecuted by his own people</li></ul>"},{"t":1680.12,"lv":3,"h":"Not pleasing God, contrary to all men","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Do not please God\"</b>: Christ in <b>John</b> - \"people will think they're <b>doing service to God</b> by killing you\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Saul of Tarsus</b> did exactly this - <b>firsthand</b></li><li class=\"d1\">thought he was pious and <b>zealous</b>, wasn't</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Contrary to all men</b>: enmity with fellow man too</li><li class=\"d1\">people <b>need to hear the gospel</b> and they try to stop it</li><li class=\"d0\">Not Paul attacking his own people or setting Christians <b>superior</b></li><li class=\"d1\">topic of <b>great pain</b> (Romans)</li><li class=\"d1\">would <b>go to hell himself</b> if it saved fellow Jews</li><li class=\"d0\">Not delighting - \"<b>sad truth</b>\"; hopeful it changes</li><li class=\"d0\">Like pre-Damascus road: made themselves <b>obstacle to grace and the gospel</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1851.51,"lv":2,"h":"2:16 - Wrath has come upon them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v16</b>: <b>forbidding us to speak to the Gentiles</b> that they may be saved → \"fill up the measure of their sins, <b>wrath has come upon them</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Core of problem: trying to <b>stop gospel to the nations</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God's wrath</b> = what happens on <b>wrong side of him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"God's really angry, gonna <b>smash them</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">fathers: <b>divine energies</b> - God at work <b>transfiguring</b> the world, people included</li><li class=\"d1\">image: <b>rushing river</b> - fight the current, it <b>tears you apart</b>; go with it, it <b>carries you</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same as <b>Romans</b> on wrath; Paul <b>not gloating</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they're <b>already suffering</b> it - consequences of fighting what God does in the world and <b>in you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul knows: if written <b>50-51</b>, he was doing it ~<b>15 years before</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not the end of their story; not \"for all descendants until end of time\"</li><li class=\"d0\">It's an <b>analogy</b>: Thessalonians ~ Judean Christians; pagans who rejected ~ unbelieving Judeans</li><li class=\"d1\">look at fellow pagans <b>as Paul looks at fellow Judeans</b>: <b>not as the enemy</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2052.39,"lv":2,"h":"2:17-18 - Wanting to come again","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v17</b>: taken away \"for a short time in <b>presence, not in heart</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"left his <b>heart</b> in Thessalonica\" - wants to <b>visit again</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v18</b>: \"time and again, but <b>Satan hindered us</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"even I, Paul\" - three co-writers, so he specifies</li><li class=\"d0\">Things keep going wrong - ascribed to <b>Satan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Satan as a <b>nuisance</b>: \"oh man, I lost my pen\"</li><li class=\"d1\">example: no matches before <b>Vespers</b> for the <b>charcoal</b>, altar servers used last - \"that kind of Satan\" - \"annoying, irritating <b>imp</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2176.67,"lv":3,"h":"Why Satan is only a nuisance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why can Paul talk so? <b>Christ already defeated him</b> - \"he's got the <b>big L</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul just proclaimed the <b>victory of Christ over Satan</b> → \"Satan's washed up\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: would a Jew do that? <b>Second Temple literature</b>: very scary devils</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Azazel, Mastema, Belial</b>, the Satan</li><li class=\"d1\">the scary guy for the <b>final showdown</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not Paul's view - even in <b>Revelation</b>: what does the dragon pull off?</li><li class=\"d1\">tricks and deceives → <b>tied up, pit for 1000 years</b> → let out, deceives again → <b>lake of fire</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"if you were making a <b>superhero movie</b>, not a good villain\" - no drama</li><li class=\"d0\">\"It's over, it wasn't close\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2311.31,"lv":2,"h":"2:19-20 - You are our hope and joy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v19</b>: \"what is our <b>hope or joy or crown of rejoicing</b>? Is it not even <b>you</b> at his <b>coming</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Back to <b>CV idea</b>: what will I <b>brag about</b> at end of life?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>you</b>, standing before Christ at the <b>second coming</b>, among the <b>righteous</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>return on investment</b> of time, love, care</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul does work out <b>own salvation</b>, but more focused on <b>others'</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I don't want to help other people find salvation and <b>not find it myself</b>\" - note <b>which comes first</b></li></ul>"}]});
